            <tr><td>Best for</td><td>Larger DTC brands with high SMS volume</td><td>Stores focused on cart recovery via mobile channels</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Pricing</td><td>Custom enterprise pricing</td><td>Paid plans / custom</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Shopify depth</td><td>Deep</td><td>Native</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Automation</td><td>Advanced</td><td>Solid</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Cart channels</td><td>sms, email, marketing, cart recovery</td><td>sms, marketing, cart recovery</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Rating</td><td>4.6/5</td><td>4.4/5</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <p>These are illustrative recovery proposals, not observed tests or verified vendor capabilities. Assume margin before the incentive, fixed product cost and an order-wide discount: contribution = AOV × (margin − discount); contribution lost = AOV × discount. Figures exclude messaging, shipping, returns, tax and other variable costs. The $677 cart at 64% margin and a 13% cap contributes $345.27 versus $433.28 at full price, a loss of $88.01.</p>
        <p>Attentive vs Recart: scenario 1 — logged-in repeat buyer with saved address. At $553 AOV and 58% margin, full-price recovery contributes $320.74 vs $215.67 after a 19% code (Δ $105.07). Ladder touch 1 favors push nudge; watch for recovery for fully OOS cart. Email 1 ~54m, email 2 ~38h, SMS branch ~4h for opted-in only.</p>
        <p>Attentive vs Recart: scenario 2 — international shipping quote sticker shock. At $553 AOV and 58% margin, full-price recovery contributes $320.74 vs $215.67 after a 19% code (Δ $105.07). Ladder touch 2 favors no-discount assist; watch for duplicate SMS and email within 20 minutes. Email 1 ~54m, email 2 ~38h, SMS branch ~4h for opted-in only.</p>
        <p>Attentive vs Recart: scenario 3 — subscription toggle left on at checkout. At $553 AOV and 58% margin, full-price recovery contributes $320.74 vs $215.67 after a 19% code (Δ $105.07). Ladder touch 3 favors email proof; watch for welcome discount stacking with cart code. Email 1 ~54m, email 2 ~38h, SMS branch ~4h for opted-in only.</p>
        <p>Attentive vs Recart: scenario 4 — first-time mobile shopper on Instagram traffic. At $553 AOV and 58% margin, full-price recovery contributes $320.74 vs $215.67 after a 19% code (Δ $105.07). Ladder touch 4 favors SMS urgency; watch for discount on email one before trust proof. Email 1 ~54m, email 2 ~38h, SMS branch ~4h for opted-in only.</p>
        <p>Attentive vs Recart: scenario 5 — size matrix with two variants OOS. At $553 AOV and 58% margin, full-price recovery contributes $320.74 vs $215.67 after a 19% code (Δ $105.07). Ladder touch 1 favors push nudge; watch for SMS after 9pm local without quiet hours. Email 1 ~54m, email 2 ~38h, SMS branch ~4h for opted-in only.</p>
        <p>Attentive vs Recart: scenario 6 — gift message field abandoned mid-flow. At $553 AOV and 58% margin, full-price recovery contributes $320.74 vs $215.67 after a 19% code (Δ $105.07). Ladder touch 2 favors no-discount assist; watch for no suppression after partial refund. Email 1 ~54m, email 2 ~38h, SMS branch ~4h for opted-in only.</p>
        <p>Attentive vs Recart: scenario 7 — high-AOV cart with financing widget opened. At $553 AOV and 58% margin, full-price recovery contributes $320.74 vs $215.67 after a 19% code (Δ $105.07). Ladder touch 3 favors email proof; watch for attribution credit on would-have-returned orders. Email 1 ~54m, email 2 ~38h, SMS branch ~4h for opted-in only.</p>
