        <h2>Cart recovery workflow test</h2>
        <p>$553 cart: email 54m / 38h / SMS 4h. $677 cart: adjust discount cap down 13% max. Exit on purchase; suppress OOS.</p>
        <h2>Channel escalation</h2>
        <p>A named lifecycle owner should verify current purchase, refund, stock, suppression, permission and local-time state before each send. Treat the 15-minute exit window as a proposed target, not permission to send against stale state. Use a stable cart/event key across channels so replays and delayed events cannot enqueue duplicate reminders; uncertain state goes to an owner-reviewed queue. Confirm each proposed channel and integration in the selected account before enabling it.</p>
        <p>Email carries proof; SMS compresses urgency; never duplicate paragraphs cross-channel. Cap 3 touches per cart per 7 days.</p>
        <h2>Attribution</h2>
        <p>Holdout 5%; measure incrementality and contribution margin after discount — compare randomized eligible groups over the same window; do not assume any fixed attribution overstatement. Assign an analyst to reconcile refunds, costs and uncertainty before interpreting lift.</p>
